1
00:00:49,049 --> 00:00:52,301
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

2
00:00:52,302 --> 00:00:54,428
- Let's have one more drink.
- You had too much already.

3
00:00:54,429 --> 00:00:56,514
6 YEARS AGO

4
00:00:56,515 --> 00:00:58,224
No, you need to go home.

5
00:00:58,225 --> 00:01:00,268
Hey, mister. Join me for a drink.

6
00:01:00,269 --> 00:01:02,061
- They won't drink with me.
- Have you gone crazy?

7
00:01:02,062 --> 00:01:03,479
- Stop it.
- Sorry.

8
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:04,605
- Go home.
- No.

9
00:01:04,606 --> 00:01:06,858
- I'm fine. Let go of me.
- You sure?

10
00:01:07,609 --> 00:01:08,860
The taxi's not here yet?

11
00:01:09,319 --> 00:01:11,070
- It's...
- Let's go drink!

12
00:01:11,071 --> 00:01:13,656
- What's wrong with you?
- What?

13
00:01:13,657 --> 00:01:14,991
- Let go.
- It's coming.

14
00:01:14,992 --> 00:01:16,158
- It's not here yet.
- It's here.

15
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:17,285
- Here it is.
- It's here?

16
00:01:17,286 --> 00:01:19,204
- It's here.
- Darn it.

17
00:01:20,122 --> 00:01:21,539
- Where are we going?
- Mapo-gu.

18
00:01:21,540 --> 00:01:23,124
- For Mapo-gu, right?
- That's where you live.

19
00:01:23,125 --> 00:01:24,333
- I live there?
- Yes.

20
00:01:24,334 --> 00:01:27,086
- Okay, I'm fine. Let go.
- Okay.

21
00:01:27,087 --> 00:01:28,338
Wait. Give me a moment.

22
00:01:29,214 --> 00:01:30,840
- Darn it.
- What now?

23
00:01:30,841 --> 00:01:32,717
- Here's 20,000 won for Seon-hyuk.
- Thank you.

24
00:01:32,718 --> 00:01:34,677
And 20,000 won for Eun-tae.

25
00:01:34,678 --> 00:01:35,970
- Take a taxi home.
- Thank you.

26
00:01:35,971 --> 00:01:37,805
- Goodbye, sir.
- Hey, I have no cash.

27
00:01:37,806 --> 00:01:40,057
- Give me 10,000 won. I'm out.
- Give me yours.

28
00:01:40,058 --> 00:01:41,560
- Mine?
- I'm all out.

29
00:01:41,935 --> 00:01:43,102
- Bye!
- No, wait.

30
00:01:43,103 --> 00:01:44,854
- Now we can afford another...
- We can't.

31
00:01:44,855 --> 00:01:47,565
That hurt, you know. It really hurt.

32
00:01:47,566 --> 00:01:50,568
- Hey, wait. My briefcase.
- Here you go.

33
00:01:50,569 --> 00:01:52,862
This isn't mine. Give me mine.

34
00:01:52,863 --> 00:01:54,780
Why are you so out of it?

35
00:01:54,781 --> 00:01:58,159
Are you sure you two
won't go drinking without me?

36
00:01:58,160 --> 00:02:00,453
- We won't. Bye.
- Are you sure?

37
00:02:00,454 --> 00:02:02,622
- Bye. See you.
- I'm serious. Don't do that.

38
00:02:02,623 --> 00:02:03,832
Take care!

39
00:02:04,124 --> 00:02:05,626
That was so freaking hard.

40
00:02:09,796 --> 00:02:11,798
It took us 30 minutes
to get him to go.

41
00:02:12,466 --> 00:02:14,508
That's way faster than before.

42
00:02:14,509 --> 00:02:16,719
He used to fall asleep on the ground.

43
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:18,888
Will you be like that
if you become a team leader?

44
00:02:18,889 --> 00:02:20,014
Why?

45
00:02:20,015 --> 00:02:22,517
Will you send me home
when I become a team leader?

46
00:02:23,018 --> 00:02:24,393
I'll do exactly that tonight.

47
00:02:24,394 --> 00:02:27,397
Hey, Gong...

48
00:02:29,650 --> 00:02:31,693
- You. Follow me.
- What?

49
00:02:32,027 --> 00:02:33,110
- Follow me.
- Why?

50
00:02:33,111 --> 00:02:34,571
- Come with me.
- Where to?

51
00:02:35,739 --> 00:02:36,990
Do you buy lottery tickets?

52
00:02:37,449 --> 00:02:39,408
I've tried it a couple of times.

53
00:02:39,409 --> 00:02:41,161
What's today's date?

54
00:02:42,412 --> 00:02:46,083
It's April 27th,
and the time is 11...

55
00:02:46,541 --> 00:02:48,000
It's 11:42 p.m.

56
00:02:48,001 --> 00:02:49,169
Forty-two.

57
00:02:49,670 --> 00:02:51,046
The last digit
of your employee number.

58
00:02:51,296 --> 00:02:53,882
My employee number...
Oh, it's an eight.

59
00:02:54,174 --> 00:02:56,092
Eight for you. Three for me.

60
00:02:56,093 --> 00:02:57,301
LOTTO, PENSION LOTTERY, SCRATCH-OFF

61
00:02:57,302 --> 00:02:59,262
The rest will be randomly generated.

62
00:03:03,684 --> 00:03:04,809
- Sir.
- Yes?

63
00:03:04,810 --> 00:03:06,769
- Two tickets with these numbers.
- Okay.

64
00:03:06,770 --> 00:03:07,771
Thanks.

65
00:03:09,398 --> 00:03:11,482
One for me, one for you.

66
00:03:11,483 --> 00:03:12,693
Thank you.

67
00:03:14,444 --> 00:03:15,487
Do you buy these often?

68
00:03:16,029 --> 00:03:17,614
Whenever I see a stall.

69
00:03:18,198 --> 00:03:19,199
Don't you?

70
00:03:19,783 --> 00:03:22,494
I don't want to get my hopes up
when I'll never win, anyway.

71
00:03:22,744 --> 00:03:24,705
Who cares if you never win?

72
00:03:25,956 --> 00:03:28,582
Do you buy them
thinking you'll win when you won't?

73
00:03:28,583 --> 00:03:32,212
Doesn't it feel like
this moment has more meaning now?

74
00:03:33,338 --> 00:03:35,214
Work is always the same.

75
00:03:35,215 --> 00:03:36,717
Life is boring.

76
00:03:36,967 --> 00:03:39,428
Buying a lottery ticket
gives time some meaning.

77
00:03:39,886 --> 00:03:42,889
That makes today worth celebrating.

78
00:03:43,348 --> 00:03:45,016
That's why I buy them.

79
00:03:46,101 --> 00:03:47,352
That's pretty romantic.

80
00:03:47,978 --> 00:03:49,312
Don't fall for me.

81
00:03:51,565 --> 00:03:52,899
You never know.

82
00:03:53,442 --> 00:03:55,192
There are eight billion people
out there.

83
00:03:55,193 --> 00:03:57,779
What's the probability
that we would ever meet?

84
00:03:59,239 --> 00:04:00,990
I don't know.

85
00:04:00,991 --> 00:04:03,201
One in 100 million?
No, one in 10 million.

86
00:04:04,244 --> 00:04:05,786
I don't know, either.

87
00:04:05,787 --> 00:04:08,622
But the chance of winning
the lottery is one in eight million.

88
00:04:08,623 --> 00:04:11,542
Doesn't that mean
the chance of us meeting

89
00:04:11,543 --> 00:04:13,712
is almost as good as the chance
that we'll win the lottery?

90
00:04:14,421 --> 00:04:16,839
You and I happened to meet.

91
00:04:16,840 --> 00:04:18,383
Who's to say we won't win?

92
00:04:20,302 --> 00:04:21,511
I say it's possible.

93
00:04:22,596 --> 00:04:24,556
If this is worth anything,
we're halving it, okay?

94
00:04:26,224 --> 00:04:27,433
Let's go home now.

95
00:04:27,434 --> 00:04:29,101
LOTTERY TICKETS

96
00:04:29,102 --> 00:04:30,270
Where's my briefcase?

97
00:04:31,104 --> 00:04:32,314
Oh, yes. Thank you.

98
00:04:36,943 --> 00:04:42,991
EPISODE 5: WHEN NO ONE SAYS
WHAT THEY REALLY FEEL

99
00:04:55,295 --> 00:04:56,629
HONGSUNG
INTERNATIONAL

100
00:04:56,630 --> 00:04:57,964
Oh, my goodness.

101
00:04:58,507 --> 00:05:00,926
Are you all here because of me?

102
00:05:01,593 --> 00:05:02,969
You get that much?

103
00:05:04,679 --> 00:05:05,847
So what is it?

104
00:05:06,765 --> 00:05:10,226
Did you rush over anxiously
to apologize for causing a mess

105
00:05:10,227 --> 00:05:11,937
or to clean it up?

106
00:05:12,687 --> 00:05:14,523
Will it all be okay if I apologize?

107
00:05:15,106 --> 00:05:16,608
Of course not, you punk.

108
00:05:17,025 --> 00:05:19,528
What should I do, then?

109
00:05:20,779 --> 00:05:21,780
I don't know.

110
00:05:22,239 --> 00:05:25,325
What do you want me to do, Mr. Jang?

111
00:05:26,451 --> 00:05:27,952
What are you even doing right now?

112
00:05:27,953 --> 00:05:29,371
Should I stay here

113
00:05:29,704 --> 00:05:33,124
wasting space and time
just waiting to be fired?

114
00:05:33,792 --> 00:05:35,669
Is that what you think you do here?

115
00:05:38,630 --> 00:05:40,298
You don't deserve to lead a team.

116
00:05:40,966 --> 00:05:43,634
I wouldn't have promoted you
if I'd known you were like this.

117
00:05:43,635 --> 00:05:44,719
I'm sorry

118
00:05:45,554 --> 00:05:48,722
but I'm not here to apologize
or clean anything up.

119
00:05:48,723 --> 00:05:50,308
You're not?

120
00:05:50,851 --> 00:05:54,062
Then how about
you explain your actions?

121
00:05:54,479 --> 00:05:55,480
Explain?

122
00:06:00,235 --> 00:06:01,820
Did I do something wrong?

123
00:06:03,822 --> 00:06:07,325
I can get why you tried to steal
one of our business partners.

124
00:06:07,993 --> 00:06:12,454
Well, I don't get it,
but Ms. Park can, so I'll let it go.

125
00:06:12,455 --> 00:06:15,833
You were there
when we signed on Mantua

126
00:06:15,834 --> 00:06:18,378
so we can say you own some equity.

127
00:06:20,130 --> 00:06:22,424
But if you want to leave,
leave alone.

128
00:06:24,092 --> 00:06:25,594
Why poach our employees?

129
00:06:26,678 --> 00:06:30,307
If Hongsung is a better company,
they'll choose to stay here.

130
00:06:30,724 --> 00:06:32,100
If not, they'll come with me.

131
00:06:33,018 --> 00:06:35,228
I can't force someone
to come with me.

132
00:06:35,729 --> 00:06:37,272
The decision is theirs to make.

133
00:06:38,315 --> 00:06:40,358
You sound so rational and reasonable.

134
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:43,570
Okay, then.
I'll respond just as rationally.

135
00:06:44,195 --> 00:06:47,490
Do you think Hongsung won't retaliate
if you quit like this?

136
00:06:50,327 --> 00:06:51,578
Oh, gosh...

137
00:06:52,537 --> 00:06:53,580
Mr. Jang.

138
00:06:54,205 --> 00:06:58,251
Do you think I have
some grudge against Hongsung?

139
00:06:58,627 --> 00:06:59,628
Who, me?

140
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:03,548
I was loyal to Hongsung

141
00:07:04,299 --> 00:07:06,217
for over a good decade.

142
00:07:07,135 --> 00:07:10,889
If I could do my job
without having to quit, I'd stay.

143
00:07:12,015 --> 00:07:14,267
If any Hongsung employee
wants to come with me

144
00:07:14,643 --> 00:07:16,227
that's only because
they feel the same.

145
00:07:16,478 --> 00:07:17,562
Let's be honest.

146
00:07:19,397 --> 00:07:21,149
Hongsung doesn't treat people well.

147
00:07:22,275 --> 00:07:25,695
I plan to do what Hongsung can't.

148
00:07:27,739 --> 00:07:29,616
- Mr. Jeong.
- Yes?

149
00:07:31,159 --> 00:07:33,787
Do you think you're any different?

150
00:07:34,371 --> 00:07:36,538
You can't even manage your own team.

151
00:07:36,539 --> 00:07:40,084
How can you start a company
that treats people well?

152
00:07:40,085 --> 00:07:41,795
That's just nonsense.

153
00:07:43,296 --> 00:07:44,880
That's for me to prove.

154
00:07:44,881 --> 00:07:46,715
- Seon-hyuk.
- Yes?

155
00:07:46,716 --> 00:07:49,970
Our industry isn't a massive ocean.
It's a tiny stream.

156
00:07:50,512 --> 00:07:53,640
Do you think your company
will survive with us as an enemy?

157
00:07:54,849 --> 00:07:56,476
Are you actually concerned about me?

158
00:07:57,394 --> 00:07:58,395
Yes.

159
00:08:00,063 --> 00:08:02,607
I'm really concerned
about the fool you are.

160
00:08:04,859 --> 00:08:07,320
Thank you for your concern.

161
00:08:08,238 --> 00:08:09,322
But today

162
00:08:09,823 --> 00:08:12,993
I came here to ask you
not to scold the employees

163
00:08:13,368 --> 00:08:17,330
that I offered a job to
because they did nothing wrong.

164
00:08:17,956 --> 00:08:19,290
Will you do that for me?

165
00:08:23,461 --> 00:08:24,462
Jeez...

166
00:08:26,715 --> 00:08:28,174
I take it that you will
and excuse myself.

167
00:08:28,425 --> 00:08:29,467
Thank you.

168
00:08:30,635 --> 00:08:31,636
Thank you.

169
00:08:40,353 --> 00:08:41,354
Hey, Gong.

170
00:08:41,980 --> 00:08:42,981
Yes?

171
00:08:43,398 --> 00:08:44,774
Lock down Mantua as soon as possible.

172
00:08:53,992 --> 00:08:56,286
So that's why Mr. Jang came to Legal.

173
00:08:56,870 --> 00:08:59,372
He asked to see
Mr. Jeong's employment contract.

174
00:08:59,748 --> 00:09:01,624
To check
for the non-compete agreement.

175
00:09:02,125 --> 00:09:03,209
Does that carry any weight?

176
00:09:03,877 --> 00:09:07,797
It does legally,
but it's hard to enforce.

177
00:09:08,256 --> 00:09:12,510
It's an awkward lawsuit
with no guarantee of winning.

178
00:09:12,761 --> 00:09:17,432
Time will pass as the trial drags on,
and time will side with Mr. Jeong.

179
00:09:22,062 --> 00:09:24,439
Do you know Ms. Park came by
a week before that?

180
00:09:24,731 --> 00:09:25,899
- Did she?
- Yes.

181
00:09:26,274 --> 00:09:28,234
She asked the same thing as Mr. Jang.

182
00:09:28,651 --> 00:09:31,154
She wasn't going
to let it slide, either.

183
00:09:31,446 --> 00:09:34,448
Of course not.
What he's doing is harming Hongsung.

184
00:09:34,449 --> 00:09:36,076
The higher-ups
are scarier than you think.

185
00:09:37,452 --> 00:09:38,578
By the way

186
00:09:39,162 --> 00:09:41,122
do you know why Ms. Park
didn't make us take action?

187
00:09:41,790 --> 00:09:42,915
No, why?

188
00:09:42,916 --> 00:09:46,086
If we make a move,
so will the Audit Team.

189
00:09:46,795 --> 00:09:49,464
Would you want to make things worse
if you were her?

190
00:09:50,090 --> 00:09:51,757
I can't say for sure

191
00:09:51,758 --> 00:09:54,469
but I think Mr. Jeong considered that
when he planned this.

192
00:09:57,764 --> 00:09:59,349
I really don't know, though.

193
00:09:59,766 --> 00:10:03,435
Should I say Mr. Jeong
is being clever

194
00:10:03,436 --> 00:10:05,230
or pitiful?

195
00:10:07,107 --> 00:10:08,525
I don't know, either.

196
00:10:09,109 --> 00:10:12,028
I want to root for him
whatever the outcome

197
00:10:12,445 --> 00:10:15,907
but he makes me want to put away
the pompoms and draw a sword.

198
00:10:20,203 --> 00:10:21,995
A multi-brand shoe store?

199
00:10:21,996 --> 00:10:23,998
Yes, it's a new project,
and it was rushed.

200
00:10:24,332 --> 00:10:26,960
Are we doing it? How come?

201
00:10:29,129 --> 00:10:30,296
I pulled something crazy.

202
00:10:30,755 --> 00:10:35,551
If you were going to do that,
you should've given us a heads-up.

203
00:10:35,552 --> 00:10:39,556
Do we have enough people to handle
Laknes and the shoe store?

204
00:10:40,265 --> 00:10:44,518
Mantua will select the brands,
and Ms. Park will clear the finances.

205
00:10:44,519 --> 00:10:47,479
Mr. Jang will help us deal
with the brands' head offices.

206
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:49,774
There shouldn't be
much actual work to do.

207
00:10:50,984 --> 00:10:52,235
Mr. Gong.

208
00:10:52,902 --> 00:10:55,947
Are we doing this
because of Mr. Jeong?

209
00:10:58,741 --> 00:10:59,742
No.

210
00:11:00,618 --> 00:11:02,203
We're doing it
because Hongsung needs us to.

211
00:11:06,457 --> 00:11:07,834
The most important thing, then.

212
00:11:08,501 --> 00:11:09,878
What's the budget?

213
00:11:14,465 --> 00:11:16,008
That's only for the first order.

214
00:11:16,009 --> 00:11:18,178
Future ones can reach ten million.

215
00:11:18,761 --> 00:11:20,095
What do you think?

216
00:11:20,096 --> 00:11:23,223
Do you think that's enough
to persuade Mantua?

217
00:11:23,224 --> 00:11:24,850
It's a decent number.

218
00:11:24,851 --> 00:11:27,353
The number's decent.
So what are you worried about?

219
00:11:27,937 --> 00:11:30,522
The Mantua guys
aren't that reasonable.

220
00:11:30,523 --> 00:11:34,569
I'm more worried
that you're close to Mr. Jeong.

221
00:11:35,153 --> 00:11:36,321
What do you think?

222
00:11:37,488 --> 00:11:40,324
Mr. Jang.
Did you forget this was my idea?

223
00:11:40,325 --> 00:11:41,326
No.

224
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:45,038
I also know
you didn't want to do this.

225
00:11:49,042 --> 00:11:50,667
I don't care about anything else.

226
00:11:50,668 --> 00:11:53,170
It'll be a huge headache

227
00:11:53,171 --> 00:11:54,714
if you can't close the deal
with this budget.

228
00:11:55,965 --> 00:11:57,342
I'll close it.

229
00:11:58,218 --> 00:11:59,219
Good.

230
00:12:01,179 --> 00:12:02,180
Eun-tae.

231
00:12:03,973 --> 00:12:05,183
This is work.

232
00:12:07,936 --> 00:12:09,103
Don't forget that.

233
00:12:09,646 --> 00:12:10,647
I won't.

234
00:12:13,900 --> 00:12:17,027
22 HOURS TO LAKNES LAUNCH

235
00:12:17,028 --> 00:12:19,655
Ms. Cha, I saw the revised version.
It looks great.

236
00:12:19,656 --> 00:12:22,491
I saw the posts,
and they all look good.

237
00:12:22,492 --> 00:12:24,451
- Oh, yes.
- Gang, Lee, and Park.

238
00:12:24,452 --> 00:12:26,746
- They didn't post the product alone.
- Yes, thanks. Bye.

239
00:12:27,830 --> 00:12:28,997
Oh, yes, hello.

240
00:12:28,998 --> 00:12:30,791
- There are 30?
- Did you get what I sent?

241
00:12:30,792 --> 00:12:32,668
- Did you open the whole box?
- Yes, about that.

242
00:12:32,669 --> 00:12:34,212
The event that you proposed.

243
00:12:34,837 --> 00:12:38,298
- Do you mind opening two more?
- Sorry for all the changes.

244
00:12:38,299 --> 00:12:40,259
I'll take you out to eat
after the launch.

245
00:12:40,260 --> 00:12:41,677
- Yes, please check.
- Bye.

246
00:12:41,678 --> 00:12:42,970
Oh, yes.

247
00:12:42,971 --> 00:12:44,847
- Thank you. Bye.
- Thank you. Bye.

248
00:12:59,570 --> 00:13:01,029
- What are you doing?
- What?

249
00:13:01,030 --> 00:13:02,698
- What?
- Sorry?

250
00:13:02,699 --> 00:13:03,866
What are you doing?

251
00:13:05,743 --> 00:13:08,037
We're taking a break.

252
00:13:09,622 --> 00:13:10,707
Are you done?

253
00:13:13,001 --> 00:13:14,002
Let's go.

254
00:13:21,801 --> 00:13:23,761
12 HOURS TO LAKNES LAUNCH

255
00:13:34,147 --> 00:13:36,399
9 HOURS TO LAKNES LAUNCH

256
00:13:43,573 --> 00:13:44,990
- Ji-hye.
- Yes?

257
00:13:44,991 --> 00:13:47,451
Watch your pace. This is a marathon.

258
00:13:47,452 --> 00:13:48,535
Okay.

259
00:13:48,536 --> 00:13:49,661
Hey, Gi-tae.

260
00:13:49,662 --> 00:13:52,205
You're too slow.
Go at least half her speed.

261
00:13:52,206 --> 00:13:54,708
This is a marathon, you see.

262
00:13:54,709 --> 00:13:57,502
- What?
- You're the slowest, Mr. Yang.

263
00:13:57,503 --> 00:13:58,796
Oh, Mr. Gong.

264
00:13:59,464 --> 00:14:01,174
Come and take a seat.

265
00:14:04,093 --> 00:14:05,552
Sorry I'm late.

266
00:14:05,553 --> 00:14:07,555
Don't be. We just got started.

267
00:14:08,222 --> 00:14:09,639
Where do I start?

268
00:14:09,640 --> 00:14:12,143
Put these stickers on there.

269
00:14:13,603 --> 00:14:16,188
Why did you join us? We could manage.

270
00:14:16,189 --> 00:14:17,898
Laknes opens tomorrow.

271
00:14:17,899 --> 00:14:20,818
- We have a final meeting too.
- Mr. Gong.

272
00:14:22,862 --> 00:14:25,530
The banners are up on the Gangnam
and Sogong-dong stores.

273
00:14:25,531 --> 00:14:27,574
We're halfway through
the influencer marketing.

274
00:14:27,575 --> 00:14:30,327
We confirmed
the opening event and supply

275
00:14:30,328 --> 00:14:32,288
and this bar code sticker job
is the last on the list.

276
00:14:35,249 --> 00:14:37,585
We leave the rest to the heavens.

277
00:14:38,878 --> 00:14:41,547
No one up there will help
stick the bar codes.

278
00:14:42,256 --> 00:14:45,593
It's crucial that we finish this
by morning.

279
00:14:45,843 --> 00:14:48,888
Heaven helps those
who help themselves.

280
00:14:49,764 --> 00:14:51,807
He keeps spouting stuff like that.

281
00:14:51,808 --> 00:14:54,101
- Come here. You need help.
- Sorry. I'll stop.

282
00:14:54,102 --> 00:14:55,811
I'll do all of this.

283
00:14:55,812 --> 00:14:57,312
- Sorry. I'll help.
- Hands off.

284
00:14:57,313 --> 00:14:59,689
- Okay, fine. Let me.
- I'll do it all.

285
00:14:59,690 --> 00:15:00,691
Excuse me.

286
00:15:01,776 --> 00:15:04,404
- Where are you going?
- Leave my share to do later.

287
00:15:05,655 --> 00:15:09,909
Hey, don't you think
he looks excited these days?

288
00:15:11,744 --> 00:15:13,162
He does.

289
00:15:31,764 --> 00:15:32,807
Good thinking.

290
00:15:43,359 --> 00:15:44,360
Yes. Bye.

291
00:15:49,949 --> 00:15:50,992
Korea?

292
00:15:51,576 --> 00:15:53,286
Yes. Hongsung.

293
00:15:53,661 --> 00:15:56,122
- Are they coming to discuss Jeong?
- Probably.

294
00:15:56,873 --> 00:15:58,249
They won't come empty-handed.

295
00:15:59,292 --> 00:16:00,334
They'll bring an armful.

296
00:16:01,544 --> 00:16:04,296
Whatever they bring,
don't touch what's mine, okay?

297
00:16:04,297 --> 00:16:06,006
You should know me by now.

298
00:16:06,007 --> 00:16:07,175
I'm disappointed.

299
00:16:14,182 --> 00:16:17,268
42 MINUTES TO LAKNES LAUNCH

300
00:16:36,412 --> 00:16:37,413
Wait here.

301
00:16:37,788 --> 00:16:40,082
- What time is it?
- It's 9:48 a.m.

302
00:16:40,917 --> 00:16:41,918
No, wait.

303
00:16:42,502 --> 00:16:44,544
We need to move two at once.

304
00:16:44,545 --> 00:16:45,755
Okay.

305
00:16:46,589 --> 00:16:47,839
That's it.

306
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:49,425
- Gi-tae.
- Let me.

307
00:16:50,009 --> 00:16:51,551
We made it on time.

308
00:16:51,552 --> 00:16:53,638
We can't say yet.
We're cutting it close.

309
00:16:55,640 --> 00:16:57,225
Hey, Ji-hye.

310
00:16:57,725 --> 00:16:59,560
- Two boxes?
- You can do it.

311
00:17:01,896 --> 00:17:03,272
I told you to wait.

312
00:17:07,610 --> 00:17:08,611
What?

313
00:17:11,197 --> 00:17:12,657
Hurry up, Ji-hye.

314
00:17:14,951 --> 00:17:15,993
Move it.

315
00:17:26,671 --> 00:17:29,048
You barely made it.
I thought we'd lost you.

316
00:17:29,423 --> 00:17:32,009
We came as soon as we could.
We were up all night.

317
00:17:32,343 --> 00:17:34,761
It wasn't my idea to get the goods
so close to opening.

318
00:17:34,762 --> 00:17:36,012
Oh, whatever. I deserve praise.

319
00:17:36,013 --> 00:17:37,765
Forget the praise and drink this.

320
00:17:38,307 --> 00:17:40,226
Thanks. I knew it was for us.

321
00:17:42,645 --> 00:17:44,479
You redid the whole display wall.

322
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:45,898
You think we weren't working?

323
00:17:46,983 --> 00:17:49,109
- Drink outside the store.
- I haven't even taken a sip.

324
00:17:49,110 --> 00:17:50,527
- Mr. Gong.
- Yes.

325
00:17:50,528 --> 00:17:51,779
Here's an iced coffee.

326
00:17:56,909 --> 00:17:58,828
The mall is open. Get ready.

327
00:18:29,775 --> 00:18:30,901
Is this the sound of footsteps?

328
00:18:31,611 --> 00:18:32,653
Are they coming to Laknes?

329
00:18:51,505 --> 00:18:54,091
Welcome. There's no need to run.

330
00:18:54,467 --> 00:18:56,135
Stay close to the wall, please.

331
00:19:00,222 --> 00:19:01,849
Take your time.

332
00:19:02,933 --> 00:19:04,226
Please wait here.

333
00:19:14,111 --> 00:19:15,571
Please wait here.

334
00:19:51,357 --> 00:19:52,358
Excuse me.

335
00:20:37,528 --> 00:20:38,529
Bye then.

336
00:20:51,083 --> 00:20:52,752
Mr. Gong, have a coffee.

337
00:20:53,461 --> 00:20:54,670
- Thanks.
- Sure.

338
00:20:57,423 --> 00:20:58,507
Did you get some rest?

339
00:20:58,799 --> 00:21:01,552
Well, yes. I'm rested up.

340
00:21:01,886 --> 00:21:03,262
Good. We're going on a business trip.

341
00:21:05,055 --> 00:21:06,056
Pardon?

342
00:21:06,348 --> 00:21:07,975
You're coming with me to Italy.

343
00:21:11,353 --> 00:21:13,188
- Am I going with you?
- Yes.

344
00:21:13,189 --> 00:21:14,523
It's time you went
on a business trip.

345
00:21:15,441 --> 00:21:17,526
Oh, okay. Got it.

346
00:21:18,444 --> 00:21:20,321
Will this be your first trip there?

347
00:21:20,738 --> 00:21:22,323
Yes, I've never been to Italy.

348
00:21:24,158 --> 00:21:25,159
What a shame.

349
00:21:25,618 --> 00:21:28,496
You're going to Italy,
but you won't get to see any of it.

350
00:21:29,163 --> 00:21:31,539
- What?
- You'll see what I mean.

351
00:21:31,540 --> 00:21:32,875
That's what business trips are like.

352
00:21:40,007 --> 00:21:41,008
Okay.

353
00:22:32,142 --> 00:22:34,103
MANTUA, ITALY

354
00:23:21,525 --> 00:23:23,319
Everything here is limited edition.

355
00:23:38,083 --> 00:23:39,084
Gi-tae?

356
00:23:49,345 --> 00:23:50,429
Mr. Gong?

357
00:23:52,473 --> 00:23:54,183
Can I ask you something?

358
00:23:54,683 --> 00:23:55,684
Of course.

359
00:23:56,936 --> 00:24:00,189
Why did you bring me on this trip?

360
00:24:02,858 --> 00:24:04,568
You asked the same thing I did.

361
00:24:06,403 --> 00:24:07,404
What?

362
00:24:08,072 --> 00:24:10,448
From now on,
when you visit an Italian warehouse

363
00:24:10,449 --> 00:24:11,825
don't be too surprised.

364
00:24:27,883 --> 00:24:30,385
It's a pleasure to meet you,
Mr. Sponza.

365
00:24:30,386 --> 00:24:31,428
It's a pleasure for me too.

366
00:24:57,037 --> 00:24:59,164
I booked a perfect restaurant.

367
00:26:45,020 --> 00:26:46,021
Give me one minute.

368
00:26:57,950 --> 00:26:59,993
I should've recorded that.

369
00:27:01,578 --> 00:27:03,080
The negotiation is not over yet.

370
00:27:03,330 --> 00:27:04,331
What?

371
00:27:04,665 --> 00:27:06,333
There's no way Sponza
would drop it like this.

372
00:27:07,751 --> 00:27:08,752
Try the coffee.

373
00:27:36,155 --> 00:27:38,824
What do you mean
the shipment's withheld?

374
00:27:39,491 --> 00:27:42,202
No, that can't be. Check again.

375
00:27:43,120 --> 00:27:45,080
What? Hello?

376
00:27:45,831 --> 00:27:46,832
Hello?

377
00:27:48,041 --> 00:27:49,751
Damn it, what the heck?

378
00:28:01,096 --> 00:28:02,471
The call cannot be connected.

379
00:28:02,472 --> 00:28:04,391
Sponza, you rascal.

380
00:28:26,788 --> 00:28:27,789
Emilio.

381
00:28:28,540 --> 00:28:29,749
I told you, Sponza.

382
00:28:29,750 --> 00:28:31,500
Don't touch what's mine.

383
00:28:31,501 --> 00:28:33,419
I heard you.
That's why I'm asking for a favor.

384
00:28:33,420 --> 00:28:34,962
I don't know how big
your Hongsung deal is

385
00:28:34,963 --> 00:28:36,298
but I cannot cancel this shipment.

386
00:28:37,883 --> 00:28:39,551
May I know the reason
you're refusing?

387
00:28:42,387 --> 00:28:43,430
He speaks Italian?

388
00:28:43,680 --> 00:28:44,681
I had no idea.

389
00:28:45,140 --> 00:28:46,641
I'm still learning.

390
00:28:46,642 --> 00:28:50,646
If I know why you're refusing,
perhaps I can help.

391
00:28:52,898 --> 00:28:55,234
Okay. My daughter designed
the products in this shipment.

392
00:28:56,360 --> 00:28:59,071
I wasn't a good father
since I divorced her mother.

393
00:28:59,696 --> 00:29:02,032
This is the first ever order
my daughter got.

394
00:29:02,824 --> 00:29:04,701
And you want me to cancel it? No way.

395
00:29:05,786 --> 00:29:07,828
May I ask what the products are?

396
00:29:07,829 --> 00:29:08,955
They're sunglasses.

397
00:29:08,956 --> 00:29:10,290
Including the sunglasses

398
00:29:10,749 --> 00:29:12,668
how much did Mr. Jeong
order in total?

399
00:29:13,043 --> 00:29:14,628
About 900,000 euros.

400
00:29:25,806 --> 00:29:26,807
I'm sorry?

401
00:29:28,684 --> 00:29:31,395
- How did that happen?
- That's how things went.

402
00:29:31,687 --> 00:29:33,814
I'll send you all the related info.

403
00:29:34,189 --> 00:29:37,276
Can you set it up so I can report it
as soon as I get back?

404
00:29:37,943 --> 00:29:41,280
I can get the papers in order,
but how did that happen?

405
00:29:42,447 --> 00:29:45,367
I had to do it to seal the deal.

406
00:29:45,575 --> 00:29:47,995
So you spent an extra 900,000 euros?

407
00:29:48,704 --> 00:29:50,371
This is insane.

408
00:29:50,372 --> 00:29:52,248
I'll explain when I get back.

409
00:29:52,249 --> 00:29:54,208
Of course, you must explain, but...

410
00:29:54,209 --> 00:29:56,253
- Do that for me.
- Hello?

411
00:29:56,962 --> 00:29:58,005
Mr. Gong?

412
00:30:02,217 --> 00:30:03,884
What's gotten into him?

413
00:30:03,885 --> 00:30:05,887
- Did he get excited again?
- Yes.

414
00:30:08,473 --> 00:30:10,934
What are you thinking, Mr. Gong?

415
00:30:12,769 --> 00:30:15,731
We did things
the Hongsung way so far.

416
00:30:16,231 --> 00:30:18,065
At least this time,
I'd like to do things my way.

417
00:30:18,066 --> 00:30:19,150
Sorry?

418
00:30:19,151 --> 00:30:21,069
The worst they can do is fire me.

419
00:30:21,903 --> 00:30:22,904
What?

420
00:30:23,238 --> 00:30:25,615
Mr. Gong!

421
00:30:44,676 --> 00:30:47,137
MISSED CALL FROM
TEAM 4 MR. JEONG SEON-HYUK

422
00:30:54,353 --> 00:30:57,188
Mr. Gong, take the taxi in front.

423
00:30:57,189 --> 00:30:59,190
- Okay.
- Bye, then.

424
00:30:59,191 --> 00:31:00,609
Good job. Get back safely.

425
00:31:01,526 --> 00:31:03,528
Can you open the trunk for me?

426
00:31:12,204 --> 00:31:13,246
Mr. Gong.

427
00:31:15,415 --> 00:31:17,459
I learned a lot on this trip.

428
00:31:19,086 --> 00:31:20,087
Thank you.

429
00:31:24,341 --> 00:31:26,009
You really are just like me.

430
00:31:26,593 --> 00:31:27,594
What?

431
00:31:30,472 --> 00:31:32,473
Never mind. See you tomorrow.

432
00:31:32,474 --> 00:31:34,184
Okay. Goodbye.

433
00:32:59,853 --> 00:33:00,854
Hey, there.

434
00:33:02,772 --> 00:33:05,025
Why are you so down?

435
00:33:05,567 --> 00:33:08,195
A CEO can't let something like this
get to him.

436
00:33:11,531 --> 00:33:12,949
Do I look down?

437
00:33:32,928 --> 00:33:34,304
Hongsung is scary.

438
00:33:35,555 --> 00:33:37,224
I'm sure you expected this.

439
00:33:38,225 --> 00:33:40,310
I didn't think they'd go this far.

440
00:33:42,020 --> 00:33:43,438
Do you blame me?

441
00:33:45,857 --> 00:33:47,108
I blame myself.

442
00:33:48,777 --> 00:33:50,779
I took you to Mantua.

443
00:33:53,907 --> 00:33:57,327
Your eyes bugged out
when you saw the warehouse.

444
00:33:57,827 --> 00:34:00,080
I taught the clueless kid everything

445
00:34:00,872 --> 00:34:02,415
and this is what he does to me.

446
00:34:04,960 --> 00:34:05,961
You told me then

447
00:34:06,461 --> 00:34:09,214
that I shouldn't act too surprised
in the warehouse.

448
00:34:11,174 --> 00:34:12,175
Did I?

449
00:34:18,098 --> 00:34:19,307
Did I go too far?

450
00:34:21,268 --> 00:34:23,895
Even if I did go too far

451
00:34:24,854 --> 00:34:26,731
do you think I deserve this?

452
00:34:37,784 --> 00:34:39,160
The multi-brand shoe store.

453
00:34:41,746 --> 00:34:43,415
Was that your idea or Hongsung's?

454
00:34:45,875 --> 00:34:47,002
It was my idea.

455
00:34:47,335 --> 00:34:48,628
Hongsung agreed.

456
00:34:50,005 --> 00:34:51,006
I see.

457
00:34:58,263 --> 00:34:59,264
Mr. Jeong.

458
00:35:01,016 --> 00:35:03,351
If I import the product,
will you buy from us?

459
00:35:04,644 --> 00:35:06,605
- What?
- But it will be

460
00:35:06,896 --> 00:35:09,608
a bit more expensive
than what Mantua asked for.

461
00:35:11,109 --> 00:35:13,652
- What are you saying?
- It's as you heard.

462
00:35:13,653 --> 00:35:16,155
You can't deal directly
with Mantua ever again.

463
00:35:16,156 --> 00:35:18,950
If you want their product,
you must buy it from Hongsung.

464
00:35:21,369 --> 00:35:22,912
The shipment is on its way.

465
00:35:23,288 --> 00:35:26,958
You can come to Hongsung this week
to sign the contract.

466
00:35:28,126 --> 00:35:29,377
I'll persuade them.

467
00:35:31,880 --> 00:35:33,214
Are you throwing me a lifeline?

468
00:35:36,217 --> 00:35:37,218
I should go.

469
00:36:03,912 --> 00:36:04,913
Hello.

470
00:36:17,384 --> 00:36:18,385
Explain.

471
00:36:19,427 --> 00:36:22,722
There was one guy who refused
to cancel his deal with Mr. Jeong.

472
00:36:24,349 --> 00:36:26,559
- Hey.
- She's the director.

473
00:36:27,102 --> 00:36:28,687
Get straight to the point.

474
00:36:30,271 --> 00:36:32,273
I didn't want to destroy Mr. Jeong.

475
00:36:35,568 --> 00:36:36,861
What about us, then?

476
00:36:37,612 --> 00:36:39,530
And the other team leaders.

477
00:36:39,531 --> 00:36:40,949
Did we want to destroy him?

478
00:36:41,866 --> 00:36:43,451
I didn't think anyone did.

479
00:36:45,537 --> 00:36:48,122
- Jeez.
- The shipment Mr. Jeong ordered

480
00:36:48,123 --> 00:36:50,333
will count as sales from our side.

481
00:36:50,667 --> 00:36:53,877
At the same time, I believe
it serves as a warning to someone

482
00:36:53,878 --> 00:36:55,839
who resigned in an abnormal manner.

483
00:36:57,632 --> 00:36:59,676
Are you saying
it works out for everyone?

484
00:36:59,926 --> 00:37:01,469
Yes, that's what I believe.

485
00:37:04,556 --> 00:37:07,600
So you went over
the agreed budget by 30%.

486
00:37:08,143 --> 00:37:10,562
Even if the order
can be counted as sales

487
00:37:11,312 --> 00:37:12,813
do you think it's okay

488
00:37:12,814 --> 00:37:15,608
to make that decision on your own
as team leader?

489
00:37:16,568 --> 00:37:19,571
What if I don't sign off on this?

490
00:37:20,822 --> 00:37:23,032
I represented Hongsung
to make a deal.

491
00:37:25,577 --> 00:37:27,412
I believe this is
the best possible result.

492
00:37:28,913 --> 00:37:29,914
Okay.

493
00:37:30,915 --> 00:37:32,959
It's on me for sending you to Mantua.

494
00:37:36,546 --> 00:37:40,007
For the time being,
report to me directly

495
00:37:40,008 --> 00:37:41,593
whenever your team places an order.

496
00:37:42,218 --> 00:37:44,179
Ask for approval before you spend
even a single won.

497
00:37:45,513 --> 00:37:46,514
Yes, ma'am.

498
00:37:48,892 --> 00:37:50,977
There's something you got wrong.

499
00:37:52,103 --> 00:37:55,398
Do you think Mr. Jeong
will be grateful for what you did?

500
00:38:08,620 --> 00:38:10,288
Is Mr. Son late again today?

501
00:38:10,830 --> 00:38:12,248
This place is a total mess.

502
00:38:21,758 --> 00:38:22,759
Gi-tae.

503
00:38:23,593 --> 00:38:24,677
(Check your phone.)

504
00:38:32,185 --> 00:38:34,687
OUR DEEPEST CONDOLENCES
HONGSUNG INTERNATIONAL

505
00:38:43,404 --> 00:38:45,198
I heard he was ill for a long time.

506
00:38:45,824 --> 00:38:48,368
He wasn't in pain when he passed.

507
00:38:49,452 --> 00:38:51,329
You should've told us.

508
00:38:52,664 --> 00:38:54,666
It's not something to brag about.

509
00:38:57,752 --> 00:38:59,003
I should've looked out for you.

510
00:38:59,754 --> 00:39:01,548
- Sorry.
- Don't be.

511
00:39:32,912 --> 00:39:34,454
CONDOLENCE MONEY BOX

512
00:39:34,455 --> 00:39:35,456
Thanks for coming.

513
00:39:35,832 --> 00:39:37,375
The deceased's son is present.

514
00:39:38,960 --> 00:39:40,169
You can go on in.

515
00:39:42,338 --> 00:39:43,548
Thanks for coming.

516
00:39:58,521 --> 00:40:00,189
Isn't work an interesting place?

517
00:40:01,274 --> 00:40:03,568
They argue all the time

518
00:40:04,402 --> 00:40:08,531
but they all help out
when things like this happen.

519
00:40:09,949 --> 00:40:12,952
Yes, I guess that keeps us going.

520
00:40:16,372 --> 00:40:19,208
I heard you'll be supplying
Mr. Jeong's company.

521
00:40:20,001 --> 00:40:21,377
Yes, that's the plan.

522
00:40:21,794 --> 00:40:22,795
You did the right thing.

523
00:40:23,922 --> 00:40:25,298
Do you really think so?

524
00:40:26,424 --> 00:40:28,300
He used to be family.

525
00:40:28,301 --> 00:40:30,511
We all know what happened.

526
00:40:31,387 --> 00:40:33,598
Hang on. Is that Mr. Jeong?

527
00:40:35,099 --> 00:40:37,226
BAEKSAN UNIVERSITY FUNERAL HALL

528
00:40:41,022 --> 00:40:42,982
- Hello.
- Hi, it's been a while.

529
00:40:43,942 --> 00:40:44,943
Hello.

530
00:40:45,860 --> 00:40:47,945
- Let's go inside.
- Not me.

531
00:40:47,946 --> 00:40:49,447
I was going to pass you this.

532
00:40:50,365 --> 00:40:51,574
Gift the money for me.

533
00:40:53,326 --> 00:40:55,369
You came all the way. Go and say hi.

534
00:40:55,370 --> 00:40:57,789
I shouldn't show myself.
Take the envelope.

535
00:41:00,166 --> 00:41:02,585
CONDOLENCE MONEY

536
00:41:10,718 --> 00:41:12,887
I'm leaving. Look after him.

537
00:41:45,211 --> 00:41:47,755
- Are you driving for Hongsung?
- Yes, Hongsung International.

538
00:41:48,131 --> 00:41:49,257
Where are the others?

539
00:41:49,966 --> 00:41:51,718
I'm the only one. Why?

540
00:41:52,010 --> 00:41:54,387
What are you on about?
All those are for Hongsung.

541
00:41:59,267 --> 00:42:01,602
- That's all for Hongsung?
- Yes.

542
00:42:02,311 --> 00:42:05,480
- It can't be.
- I'm serious. It's all theirs.

543
00:42:05,481 --> 00:42:07,108
Call someone to check.

544
00:42:07,400 --> 00:42:09,026
- Can I have more soju?
- More soju?

545
00:42:09,027 --> 00:42:11,529
- Yes.
- Just a moment. Ji-hye?

546
00:42:11,863 --> 00:42:12,864
Ji-hye.

547
00:42:13,531 --> 00:42:15,616
I'll get it for you right away.

548
00:42:17,035 --> 00:42:18,618
- Thank you.
- Sure.

549
00:42:18,619 --> 00:42:21,247
LEE MIN-HO, HONGSUNG DISTRIBUTION

550
00:42:24,333 --> 00:42:29,255
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

551
00:42:41,350 --> 00:42:43,310
6 YEARS AGO

552
00:42:43,311 --> 00:42:45,188
- Hello, Mr. Jang.
- Hi.

553
00:42:46,064 --> 00:42:47,439
Did you have a drink last night?

554
00:42:47,440 --> 00:42:48,940
Yes, I did.

555
00:42:48,941 --> 00:42:50,193
How much did you drink?

556
00:42:50,985 --> 00:42:52,361
An effing crazy amount.

557
00:42:53,071 --> 00:42:55,698
Then I'll make you
a nice cup of hot honey tea.

558
00:42:56,491 --> 00:42:57,950
Thanks so much.

559
00:43:03,873 --> 00:43:05,249
Darn it.

560
00:43:06,084 --> 00:43:07,460
- Hey.
- Yes?

561
00:43:08,878 --> 00:43:10,171
Do you buy lottery tickets?

562
00:43:10,838 --> 00:43:11,923
Sometimes.

563
00:43:12,548 --> 00:43:15,134
Don't buy them sometimes.
Buy one every week.

564
00:43:15,843 --> 00:43:17,261
We're both office workers.

565
00:43:18,096 --> 00:43:19,930
This is our only hope.

566
00:43:19,931 --> 00:43:20,932
LOTTO
5270TH DRAWING

567
00:43:22,558 --> 00:43:23,559
Hey.

568
00:43:24,602 --> 00:43:25,727
You won something?

569
00:43:25,728 --> 00:43:27,605
SORRY, YOU DID NOT WIN

570
00:43:29,816 --> 00:43:31,609
Of course, I'm damn unlucky.

571
00:43:32,860 --> 00:43:33,986
Oh, whatever.

572
00:43:34,570 --> 00:43:35,988
Cheer up, Mr. Jang.

573
00:43:37,615 --> 00:43:39,325
STAFF GONG EUN-TAE

574
00:43:41,202 --> 00:43:43,996
- We're having jjamppong for lunch.
- Thank you.

575
00:43:45,623 --> 00:43:48,668
- Mr. Jang has a hangover?
- Yes, he drank an effing lot.

576
00:43:50,837 --> 00:43:52,130
Did you check your lottery ticket?

577
00:43:52,713 --> 00:43:54,048
We halve the winnings, okay?

578
00:43:54,882 --> 00:43:57,050
It'll be a dud. Did you check?

579
00:43:57,051 --> 00:43:58,427
I will now.

580
00:43:59,971 --> 00:44:01,931
CONGRATULATIONS
TOTAL WINNINGS: 50,000 WON

581
00:44:04,142 --> 00:44:06,060
- It's a dud, right?
- What?

582
00:44:06,519 --> 00:44:08,729
Yeah. Shoot.

583
00:44:10,690 --> 00:44:11,858
Of course, I'm damn unlucky.

584
00:44:14,652 --> 00:44:16,279
It's hard to win this thing.

585
00:46:49,515 --> 00:46:51,475
Subtitles by Jennifer Jean Lim
